  "window": "Oct. 29 – Nov. 1, 2026",
  "summary": "Fairbanks Police have added two arrests to their Oct. 31 bulletin, which had previously shown none: a criminal trespass arrest on Old Steese Highway and a driving-while-revoked arrest on Sixteenth Avenue. Three court files that were opened and closed on Oct. 31 without a charging document, and one closed the same day as a duplicate, are no longer searchable in the Alaska Court System's online case database, although the court's weekly filings report still lists all four. The Alaska Court System's weekly criminal filings report has been updated to cover Oct. 25 to Oct. 31 and lists 38 Fairbanks cases, four at Nenana, two at Delta Junction and none at Healy; it includes all eight cases opened inside the area on Oct. 31. The weekly dispositions report has not been updated since Oct. 26, so cases closed since then cannot be read from it. Alaska State Troopers reported no Interior incidents on Nov. 1 as of early morning, and no new criminal case was filed at any of the four area courthouses after Saturday afternoon.",
  "commentary": null,
