      "title": "Four court files closed on Oct. 31 are no longer searchable in the state case database",
      "body": [
        "Four criminal case numbers that the Alaska Court System's online case database served on Oct. 31 return no records when searched on Nov. 1.",
        "Three of them — 4FA-26-02202CR, 4FA-26-02206CR and 4DJ-26-00067CR — were opened and closed on Oct. 31, each with a single docket entry stating that no complaint or citation was filed. No charge stands against anyone on those files. The fourth, 4FA-26-02197CR, was closed the same day as a duplicate; the drunk-driving charges it had been opened for are filed under case 4FA-26-02203CR.",
        "The court system's weekly criminal filings report, run at 9:01 p.m. on Oct. 31, lists all four case numbers with the defendants' names. Two earlier case numbers, 4FA-26-02165CR and 4FA-26-02171CR, stopped being served by the database in the same way on Oct. 27, and both had also been closed the day before.",
        "Readers looking up any of these numbers in the public case database will find nothing."
      ],
